WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:17.169
Henry and his friends waited for a while.

2
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:21.387
But Mrs. Sweet didn't come out from the back room of the Sweet Shop.

3
00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:24.254
Finally they gave up and left.

4
00:00:24.255 --> 00:00:29.231
"We should go see how Nathan is doing at the lemonade stand," Henry said.

5
00:00:29.232 --> 00:00:32.084
"We've been gone for a long time."

6
00:00:32.085 --> 00:00:40.198
The others agreed.

7
00:00:40.199 --> 00:00:45.194
Back at the stand, Nathan was serving lemonade to some construction workers.

8
00:00:45.195 --> 00:00:49.061
"Hi, guys," Nathan greeted his friends as the men left.

9
00:00:49.062 --> 00:00:53.363
"Business has been great today! How's the mystery going?"

10
00:00:53.364 --> 00:00:56.467
"Not so great," Henry admitted.

11
00:00:56.468 --> 00:00:59.667
He and his friends told Nathan about the case.

12
00:00:59.668 --> 00:01:05.352
"Wow," Nathan said. "That's weird that Mrs. Sweet rushed off like that."

13
00:01:05.353 --> 00:01:09.583
"Yeah," Cole agreed. "She acted like she was guilty."

14
00:01:09.584 --> 00:01:12.892
"But she's not guilty," Maggie insisted.

15
00:01:12.893 --> 00:01:18.194
"She's way too nice to be a flavor thief! We have to prove she didn't do it!"

16
00:01:18.195 --> 00:01:22.073
"That means we have to prove that someone else did do it," Cole said.

17
00:01:22.074 --> 00:01:27.159
"Like Robby, for instance. He seemed really mad at Mr. Tate."

18
00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:35.238
"Yeah!" Maggie said. "Maybe he hates Mr. Tate so much that he tricked Mrs. Sweet into inventing that flavor!"

19
00:01:35.239 --> 00:01:38.456
"How would he do that?" Nathan asked.

20
00:01:38.457 --> 00:01:41.623
"I don't know." Maggie shrugged.

21
00:01:41.624 --> 00:01:45.131
"But I know Mrs. Sweet didn't do anything wrong."

22
00:01:45.132 --> 00:01:51.784
Henry sighed. "I like Mrs. Sweet too, Maggie. But we have to be logical.

23
00:01:51.785 --> 00:01:56.380
Mrs. Sweet has a good motive to cause trouble for the Dessert Den.

24
00:01:56.381 --> 00:02:02.714
And don't forget, she has the exact same flavor right there on her sign.

25
00:02:02.715 --> 00:02:07.362
Plus, she acted weird when we asked her about it just now."

26
00:02:07.363 --> 00:02:10.006
"All that stuff is true," Cole said.

27
00:02:10.007 --> 00:02:14.422
"If Mrs. Sweet was mean, I'd definitely think she was the thief.

28
00:02:14.423 --> 00:02:18.565
But how could someone who seems so nice do something so rotten?"

29
00:02:18.566 --> 00:02:22.920
Henry shrugged. He didn't have an answer for Cole's question.

30
00:02:22.921 --> 00:02:27.218
"Maybe you guys should go talk to Mr. Tate again," Nathan suggested.

31
00:02:27.219 --> 00:02:30.880
"That might give you some new ideas about the case.

32
00:02:30.881 --> 00:02:36.169
I'll keep watching the lemonade stand if you want. I can use the extra money."

33
00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:39.935
Maggie groaned. "It's so hot out.

34
00:02:39.936 --> 00:02:43.834
Do we really have to ride all the way back to West Belltown?"

35
00:02:43.835 --> 00:02:47.521
"If you want to clear Mrs. Sweet's name, we do," Cole said.

36
00:02:47.522 --> 00:02:56.004
"Come on, let's go."

37
00:02:56.005 --> 00:03:07.685
When The Lemonade Detectives reached the Dessert Den, Mr. Tate saw them coming and hurried to unlock the door.

38
00:03:07.686 --> 00:03:10.385
"Did you solve the case?" he asked.

39
00:03:10.386 --> 00:03:13.551
"Did Mrs. Sweet admit that she stole my flavor?"

40
00:03:13.552 --> 00:03:20.113
"Not exactly," Henry said. "We didn't get to talk to her for very long."

41
00:03:20.114 --> 00:03:27.413
Mr. Tate frowned. "Well, once you kids finally get her to admit she's guilty, I'll pay your five-dollar detective fee."

42
00:03:27.414 --> 00:03:31.154
"We still don't believe she did it!" Maggie blurted out.

43
00:03:31.155 --> 00:03:36.195
She glanced at Henry and Cole with a frown. "At least I don't."

44
00:03:36.196 --> 00:03:39.449
"Huh?" Mr. Tate looked confused.

45
00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:43.820
"We have a few theories," Henry explained calmly.

46
00:03:43.821 --> 00:03:49.729
"We need to rule out other suspects before we can be sure Mrs. Sweet is the culprit."

47
00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:55.729
"Other suspects?" Mr. Tate folded his arms across his chest. "Like who?"

48
00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:58.954
"Um, there's this kid, Robby," Cole said.

49
00:03:58.955 --> 00:04:03.208
"He seems to hate the Dessert Den. We're not sure why."

50
00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:07.432
"Yeah," Maggie put in. "Or it could all be a coincidence.

51
00:04:07.433 --> 00:04:11.883
The flavor bubble gum banana swirl isn't that unique, you know."

52
00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:16.323
Mr. Tate rolled his eyes. "Look, my grand opening is tomorrow.

53
00:04:16.324 --> 00:04:18.591
I don't have time to fool around.

54
00:04:18.592 --> 00:04:21.933
Do you want to solve this case or not?" he asked.

55
00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:25.514
"If you don't, I can find someone else to help me.

56
00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:30.107
Like the police, for instance. Or maybe I'll go to the press.

57
00:04:30.108 --> 00:04:33.945
I heard there's an award-winning investigative reporter in this town.

58
00:04:33.946 --> 00:04:36.779
Maybe he can figure out what's going on."

59
00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.412
Henry realized Mr. Tate was talking about his father.

60
00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:44.880
"The Lemonade Detectives will solve your case," he said.

61
00:04:44.881 --> 00:04:49.998
"No matter what." He gave Cole and Maggie a shove toward the door.

62
00:04:49.999 --> 00:04:54.193
"Come on, guys. Let's get back to work."

63
00:04:54.194 --> 00:04:56.319
Soon they were outside again.

64
00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.780
"What was that all about, Henry?" Maggie asked.

65
00:04:59.781 --> 00:05:01.939
"Why'd you rush us out of there?

66
00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:06.152
I thought we were going to ask Mr. Tate more questions about the case."

67
00:05:06.153 --> 00:05:09.709
"We can't let him go to the police," Henry said.

68
00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:13.188
"Or ask my dad to investigate either."

69
00:05:13.189 --> 00:05:15.363
"Why not?" Cole asked.

70
00:05:15.364 --> 00:05:19.258
"Maybe your dad can help us prove that Mrs. Sweet is innocent."

71
00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:21.550
"Maybe," Henry said.

72
00:05:21.551 --> 00:05:26.723
"But if people hear he's investigating her, they might assume she's guilty.

73
00:05:26.724 --> 00:05:30.253
And that would probably be bad for her business."

74
00:05:30.254 --> 00:05:35.524
Suddenly Maggie gasped. "That's it!" she cried.

75
00:05:35.525 --> 00:05:38.424
"I have a new theory about what's going on!

76
00:05:38.425 --> 00:05:41.855
If we can prove it, it'll clear Mrs. Sweet's name!"

77
00:05:41.856 --> 00:05:45.374
"Really? What's your theory?" Cole asked.

78
00:05:45.375 --> 00:05:49.612
"We've been taking Mr. Tate's word about what happened," Maggie said.

79
00:05:49.613 --> 00:05:55.799
"But what if he's lying? What if he's the one who stole that flavor?"
